From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: allow clearing HTT statistics selection

The default selector is zero, but a collector cannot restore this state
because writes reject zero as if they issued a firmware reset. This file
only stores a selection; the separate htt_stats_reset file sends resets.
Accept zero so temporary statistics queries can leave the prior state
unchanged, without clearing firmware counters. Keep a trailing NUL for
a maximum-length write, and reject whitespace-only input (sscanf EOF)
before it can use an uninitialized selector.

Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/debugfs_htt_stats.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/debugfs_htt_stats.c
@@ -6193,7 +6193,7 @@
 	if (count > size)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
-	char *buf __free(kfree) = kzalloc(size, GFP_KERNEL);
+	char *buf __free(kfree) = kzalloc(size + 1, GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (!buf)
 		return -ENOMEM;
 
@@ -6202,11 +6202,13 @@
 
 	num_args = sscanf(buf, "%u %u %u %u %u\n", &type, &cfg_param[0],
 			  &cfg_param[1], &cfg_param[2], &cfg_param[3]);
-	if (!num_args || num_args > 5)
+	if (num_args < 1 || num_args > 5)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
-	if (type == ATH12K_DBG_HTT_EXT_STATS_RESET ||
-	    type >= ATH12K_DBG_HTT_NUM_EXT_STATS)
+	/* Zero restores the unselected state; only htt_stats_reset sends
+	 * a firmware counter reset. No request is sent by this selector.
+	 */
+	if (type >= ATH12K_DBG_HTT_NUM_EXT_STATS)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
 	wiphy_lock(ath12k_ar_to_hw(ar)->wiphy);
